# 8. AUTHENTICATION & SECURITY

Implement secure administrator authentication.

Requirements:

- Password hashing using bcrypt.
- Secure authentication.
- HTTP-only cookies.
- Proper session expiration.
- Server-side authorization.
- Role-based access where needed.
- Protected admin routes.
- Rate limiting.
- Helmet security headers.
- Strict CORS configuration.
- Input validation.
- File upload validation.
- Secure error responses.
- Environment variable protection.

Prefer secure cookie-based authentication with properly configured session handling and CSRF protection for state-changing requests.

Never store plaintext passwords.

Never expose secrets in frontend JavaScript.

Do not create a public admin registration endpoint.

Provide a secure one-time admin creation or seeding procedure.

